[{"class":"Package","id":"3c5e2d85-e2bd-4d98-82d2-27339ad285b5","name":"banking-rar-idv-in-pdp","deploymentPackageVersion":1,"applicationName":"Symphonic admin-point-application","applicationVersion":"11.1.0.0","dateCreated":"2026-08-07T10:07:40.651319Z","createdBy":"admin","snapshotId":"377b988a-ddc6-49f9-baf9-794081ca1fd6","snapshotMessage":"Move the step-up and mDL gates fully into the PDP\n\nThree changes, all removing the PDP's dependence on booleans pre-computed by the\nGo authzen-adapter:\n\n1. Rule \"Require step-up for large payment\" (4057cc49) - dropped the\n   rar_amount_ok && rar_creditor_ok disjunct. Remaining: staff-approval acr +\n   scope, or consent_covered via the ConsentDirectory PIP.\n\n2. Rule \"Require a DEVICE-SIGNED consent...\" (f615cc34, disabled) - dropped the\n   same pair, there as NOT(rar_amount_ok AND rar_creditor_ok).\n\n3. Attribute identity_proofing_present (d12763b5) - removed the 'request'\n   resolver that took precedence over the ProofingDirectory PIP. The PDP now\n   asks the directory itself and cannot be told the answer. defaultValue stays\n   \"false\", so an unreachable directory denies.\n\nAlso fixes a latent bug exposed by (3): ServiceDefinition ProofingDirectory\n(c2afe2f7) templated its subject from agentId, but the directory keys proofing\nactivities by the customer, and the Go adapter's equivalent call uses\nonBehalfOf. As written the lookup could never match, so the gate could never\nopen. Now templated from onBehalfOf, same as ConsentDirectory.\n\nVerified in the PAP decision tester against the live directories:\n  $600 + rar_amount_ok=true + rar_creditor_ok=true\n      -> DENY + step-up-required (was an automatic PERMIT)\n  $600 + acr=staff-approval + scope banking:payments:transfer -> PERMIT\n  $300 to EXT-9999 WITH identity_proofing_present=true supplied\n      -> DENY + identity-proofing-required; trace shows the request value\n         ignored and GET /proofing/present?subject=alice&account=EXT-9999\n         